    <!-- help pages for problems -->
    <string name="help_button">What can I do?</string>
    <string name="help_what">What happened</string>
    <string name="help_try">What to try</string>
    <string name="help_details">Details</string>
    <string name="help_copy">Copy details</string>
    <string name="help_copied">Copied</string>
    <string name="help_unreachable_title">Can\'t reach the console</string>
    <string name="help_unreachable_what">Nothing answers at the console\'s address.</string>
    <string name="help_unreachable_try">• Check the IP address on the PS5 (Settings &gt; Network &gt; Connection Status). It can change after a restart.\n• Wake the console fully. Rest mode often turns the network off.\n• Use the same Wi-Fi on both. Guest networks and VPNs block it.</string>
    <string name="help_port_title">That service isn\'t running</string>
    <string name="help_port_what">The console answered, but nothing listens on that port.</string>
    <string name="help_port_try">• Start etaHEN on the console. It provides the installer (12800), the loader (9021) and FTP (1337).\n• A separate FTP payload usually uses 2121. Enter the same port here.\n• On the console card, the light that is off shows what is missing.</string>
    <string name="help_login_title">FTP login refused</string>
    <string name="help_login_what">The console\'s FTP server rejected the user name or password.</string>
    <string name="help_login_try">• etaHEN accepts the user name anonymous with any password.\n• If you set a login on the console, enter it under Upload.\n• The password isn\'t saved. Enter it again after restarting the app.</string>
    <string name="help_dropped_title">The connection dropped</string>
    <string name="help_dropped_what">The link to the console broke or stopped moving data. The app retries and continues where it stopped.</string>
    <string name="help_dropped_try">• Keep the phone near the router and the console awake.\n• Pause other big downloads on the network.\n• If it keeps failing, wait a moment and tap Try again.</string>
    <string name="help_refused_title">The installer didn\'t take the link</string>
    <string name="help_refused_what">The console is reachable, but its installer refused this link.</string>
    <string name="help_refused_try">• The link must lead straight to the package file and open without a login.\n• The console must be able to reach it. Links from this phone only work on the same Wi-Fi.\n• Check that the installer is running and the console has free space.</string>
    <string name="help_storage_title">The console stopped storing</string>
    <string name="help_storage_what">The console kept less than was sent. The drive is usually full or read-only.</string>
    <string name="help_storage_try">• Free some space on the console.\n• Choose another folder, for example on a USB drive.\n• Then tap Try again.</string>
    <string name="help_denied_title">That folder or file was refused</string>
    <string name="help_denied_what">The FTP server can\'t open, write or change it here.</string>
    <string name="help_denied_try">• Check that the folder exists. Names are case-sensitive.\n• System folders are read-only. Use /data or a USB drive.\n• A file used by a running game may be locked. Close the game.</string>
    <string name="help_phone_title">The phone can\'t use the file</string>
    <string name="help_phone_what">The file is gone or moved, the app lost access to it, or the phone is out of space.</string>
    <string name="help_phone_try">• Choose the file again.\n• Free some storage on the phone.\n• For a file in a cloud app, save it to the phone first.</string>
    <string name="help_link_title">The download link failed</string>
    <string name="help_link_what">The website did not hand over the file. The link may have expired, need a login, or the site is busy.</string>
    <string name="help_link_try">• Start the download again from the Web tab. That keeps your login.\n• Links from file-hosting sites often expire after a few minutes.\n• If the site reported an error in the 500s, try again later.</string>

